{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nCut the next minor release, 0.13.0, from reviewed main using docs/releasing.md. Prior package/tag: 0.12.0/v0.12.0. PyPI is immutable; publication uses the dispatch-from-main workflow and its pypi environment approval. Release date 2026-08-28. Closed ticket grassgreen-unfearful-quoll (4dd2-4217-318a-4613) is the 0.12.0 precedent, not duplicate work. CHANGELOG's [Unreleased] already holds curated entries (the BigInt-serialization breaking change), so step 1a is a retitle to [0.13.0] - 2026-08-28 (fresh [Unreleased], compare links updated), not a regeneration.\n\n## Plan\n- Fresh worktree from origin/main; confirm prerequisites, identity, Gerrit rights, channel state.\n- Bump pyproject.toml + every server.json version to 0.13.0; regenerate uv.lock; retitle CHANGELOG's curated [Unreleased] to [0.13.0] - 2026-08-28 with fresh [Unreleased] and compare links.\n- Preflight: version-lockstep guard, release tests, lint, typecheck, full tests, build, twine.\n- Commit with DCO + Change-Id + rebar-ticket trailer; Gerrit review to LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with no unresolved comments; Submit.\n- Dispatch release.yml from main with version=0.13.0; obtain the pypi environment approval; monitor to a terminal result.\n- Verify PyPI + PEP 740 provenance, GitHub tag/release + artifacts, MCP Registry, Homebrew tap bump (trigger autobump).\n- Channel-install nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.0 and run the packaged post-publication probe.\n- Record receipts on this ticket; close only after all acceptance criteria are met.\n\n## File impact\n- pyproject.toml — package version bump\n- server.json — MCP manifest/package version bump\n- uv.lock — root package version lockstep with pyproject.toml\n- CHANGELOG.md — retitled curated 0.13.0 release section and compare links\n\n## Rollback / failure policy\nBefore publish: stop on any failed guard/review/CI vote; remediate via a new Gerrit patchset. After publish PyPI cannot be replaced: yank 0.13.0, de-list its GitHub Release, cut a fixed patch version; never overwrite artifacts or retag published content.\n\n## Testing\n- `python scripts/release_guards.py version-lockstep --version 0.13.0 --pyproject pyproject.toml --server-json server.json`\n- `make lint && make typecheck && make test`\n- `python -m build && python -m twine check dist/*`\n- `uvx pypi-attestations verify pypi --repository https://github.com/navapbc/rebar` on the published wheel\n- `REBAR=\"$(pipx environment --value PIPX_BIN_DIR)/rebar\" python scripts/probe_rebar.py` against the channel-installed 0.13.0 build\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] pyproject.toml declares version 0.13.0.\n- [ ] server.json top-level version is 0.13.0.\n- [ ] Every server.json packages[].version is 0.13.0.\n- [ ] uv.lock records the root nava-rebar package at version 0.13.0 and `uv lock --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md contains a hand-curated 0.13.0 section dated 2026-08-28.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md has a fresh Unreleased section and correct 0.13.0 compare links.\n- [ ] `python scripts/release_guards.py version-lockstep --version 0.13.0 --pyproject pyproject.toml --server-json server.json` exits 0.\n- [ ] Release-specific guard and workflow tests exit 0 (`pytest tests/unit/test_release_guards.py tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py`).\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] `make test` exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] `python -m build` produces the 0.13.0 wheel and sdist.\n- [ ] `python -m twine check dist/*` exits 0 for the built artifacts.\n- [ ] The release commit contains DCO sign-off, a Gerrit Change-Id, and this rebar-ticket trailer.\n- [ ] Gerrit records LLM-Review +1 on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit records Verified +1 on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit has no unresolved comments on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit submits the release change and the resulting commit is on main.\n- [ ] release.yml is dispatched from main with version input 0.13.0.\n- [ ] The required pypi environment deployment is approved.\n- [ ] Every required release.yml job completes successfully.\n- [ ] PyPI serves nava-rebar 0.13.0.\n- [ ] `uvx pypi-attestations verify pypi` on the published 0.13.0 wheel with --repository https://github.com/navapbc/rebar exits 0.\n- [ ] GitHub tag v0.13.0 resolves to the released main commit.\n- [ ] GitHub Release v0.13.0 is marked Latest and attaches the 0.13.0 wheel and sdist.\n- [ ] MCP Registry reports io.github.navapbc/rebar version 0.13.0.\n- [ ] Homebrew tap Formula/rebar.rb points to the 0.13.0 PyPI sdist URL with matching SHA-256 (or scheduled autobump confirmed).\n- [ ] A fresh channel install of nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.0 passes scripts/probe_rebar.py with zero failures.\n- [ ] Release receipts, any exceptions, and the rollback disposition are recorded on this ticket."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787938036337865111,"uuid":"50a7a9e2-a230-4f44-ac7e-91b03b967e8b"}